Subject: [PATCH] P-008: validate JSON without copying the input

YYJSON_READ_VALIDATE_ONLY does not keep string bytes, but yyjson_read_opts
still copied the input so the string reader could NUL-terminate in place
and so readers could look past eof. Read the caller buffer directly.
Strings are checked by a non-mutating scanner. Numbers, NaN/Inf, and
literals near eof use a padded tail. A number that runs to eof is copied
too, because read_num looks one byte past the token. The BOM check and
the truncated-UTF-8 check read only bytes that exist. The stub doc's
str_pool stays NULL.

